      ],
      "text": "**Keeping them home today is reasonable**, especially if either child has asthma, wheezing, or other breathing problems. The latest KL readings I found for **Saturday, October 17** were around **API 161–162**—unhealthy, but below Malaysia’s reported school-closure threshold of 200. Outdoor school activities should stop once API exceeds 100, and parents may keep children home over health concerns if they notify the school. ([semakapi.my](https://semakapi.my/en/kuala-lumpur?utm_source=openai))\n\nSo: **school isn’t automatically required to close, but you can choose to keep them home**—and I’d lean that way for a child who’s sensitive to haze. Check your school’s notice and the latest reading for your nearest station before deciding, as levels can change. ([web26.bernama.com](https://web26.bernama.com/en/general/news.php?id=2620854))",
